    description: "FOUND 2026-09-26, INV-duzom's residual (PR #1229). A fully-qualified call through a THIRD-PARTY crate with no `use` statement, e.g. `serde_json::from_str(s)` or `tokio::fs::read(p)` (edition-2018 extern crates are in scope by name), still keeps the whole path in the NAME slot with the external sentinel module: rust:external:0-0:serde_json::from_str. INV-duzom splits only paths rooted at std/core/alloc (or a leading ::), because at the analyzer's external-call arm a crate name cannot be told from a local module name without the manifest, and a local `utils::helper` split into module `utils` would be a relative path posing as an owner.\n\nWHAT IT NEEDS: the crate's declared dependency names (Cargo.toml [dependencies], plus renames `package = ...`, plus workspace inheritance) available to the rust analyzer, so a head that names a dependency is absolute. Frequency NOT measured; the tokio::fs / serde_json shapes are the likely I/O-relevant ones."  # 9eb4
    fields: {}  # 9eb4
